# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 10: TEXT BACK

**Route:** `/mctb/setup/text-back` | **Wizard:** Setup Step 4 (spec 07)  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-10-TEXT-BACK.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–09

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Text Back (`/mctb/setup/text-back`, wizard text-back step).

## Primary job

Configure **customer-facing recovery message sequence** — preview, variants, variables, encoding — matching actual runtime/compliance flow.

## Press-1 mode (LOCKED)

```
Message 1 — System compliance confirmation (LOCKED, Transovo-authored, versioned)
Message 2 — Conversation opener (editable where supported)
```

Two distinct preview bubbles. Never merge into one editable "First Text."

## Existing Consent mode

Hide Press-1 system confirmation. Show only applicable recovery message flow.

## Page scope

**Owns:** opener template, initial delay (if supported), variables, link insertion, segment preview, canonical renderer preview

**Does not own:** consent mode/editor, Press-1 audio, sender registration, forwarding, campaigns, inbox replies, **business-hours variants** (removed — spec 12), cooldown/pause (→ Recovery Controls)

## Consent & sender context

Show compact consent method + link to Setup → Consent. Show sender readiness separately — valid message ≠ ready sender ≠ recipient consent.

## Key rules

- One canonical message renderer for preview + production
- Centralized compliance copy/version for system confirmation
- One recovery opener — **no** business-hours/after-hours variants (spec 12)
- Cooldown/repeat sends → Recovery Controls (`/mctb/setup/recovery`)
- Template changes apply to future sends only
- GSM-7/Unicode-aware segment count if shown
- System confirmation before opener (runtime ordering)

## Prohibited

Editable compliance message, fake AI rewrite, naive 160-char limit, duplicate schedule/sender/consent editors, preview ≠ production, campaign/bulk controls

## Definition of done

See full spec §84 checklist.

